  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1100 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nHigh pressure will scoot eastward by Thursday and a moisture \nstarved shortwave/cold front is progged to move through the region\nThursday. This could perhaps get a breeze going while we warm \nwell in to the 80s. Otherwise, no rain is expected with this \npassing system. Overall the pattern will continue to feature a\nbroad northwesterly flow aloft and presence of high pressure and\ndry air through Friday. However, guidance continues to suggest an\ninflux of tropical moisture advecting into the region from the\nGulf along with an associated low pressure system. This favors \nmedium rain chances with a few storms this weekend.",
